# AI development rules

## Canonical ranking

```ts
import { computeFundingFit } from "@/lib/ai/intelligence/funding-fit";
```

- Production match ordering and Fit Score cards use `computeFundingFit` / `rankFundingsForResearcher`
- **Never** copy Fit Score formula into tools, UI, or a second module
- Phase B (`assessExpertiseFundingMatch`, etc.) = relevance / confidence / eligibility explanations

## Assistant pipeline

- Entry: `src/app/api/assistant` → `src/lib/ai/pipeline.ts` + `router.ts` + `src/lib/ai/tools/*`
- Preserve citation and tool-result shapes in `src/lib/ai/types.ts`
- Reuse `expandQueryTokens` / text utils; keep prompts and tool Thai explanations consistent

## Expertise (Phase A)

- Evidence-weighted profiles; invalid/missing model output still yields safe fallbacks where implemented
- Do not show unverified `ai_profile` as approved expertise on public researcher pages
- Admin review flow owns approve/reject/edit of `display_profile`

## Matching (Phase B)

- Profile input: `selectProfileForMatching` — ignore `ai_profile`
- Ignore `insufficient_evidence` topics for relevance
- Eligibility must quote call text; missing researcher facts → `unknown`, not ineligible
- Sparse funding `details` capped per existing engine rules

## Funding intelligence

- Attachment text extraction feeds matching + assistant; no OCR for scanned PDFs unless explicitly scoped
- Keep extraction store helpers in `src/lib/funding-intelligence/`

## Tests to prefer

- `npm run matching:test`
- `npm run expertise:test`
- `npm run funding:test-extraction`
- `npm run funding:test-match-route`
- `npm run matching:benchmark` when changing rank/explain behavior
